messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S06
Scenario title: Vendor Meeting and Improvement Action Follow-up
Initial workflow description:
The team meets with an equipment vendor to discuss improvement ideas. After the meeting, someone summarizes the discussion and follows up on action items.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or condition triggers the scheduling of a vendor meeting — is it recurring on a fixed schedule, initiated by an internal request, or prompted by a specific operational event such as equipment underperformance?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "Which specific roles or job functions are expected to attend the vendor meeting, and which role is responsible for producing the post-meeting summary?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Is there a defined template or structured format that must be followed when writing the meeting summary, or is it created in free-form using whatever tool the author prefers?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "How are action items captured and assigned during or after the meeting — for example, are they recorded in a spreadsheet, a project management tool, or an email thread, and who is responsible for assigning ownership and due dates?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What method is used to follow up on open action items — are reminders sent manually, through an automated system, or via scheduled review meetings, and is there an escalation path if an item is overdue?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "What criteria must be met for the entire follow-up process to be considered complete — does every action item need to be individually closed and confirmed, or is there a sign-off step by a specific role?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Coordinate a vendor meeting, capture improvement decisions, and track follow-up actions.",
  "actors": [
    "equipment engineer",
    "vendor representative",
    "meeting organizer",
    "action-item owner",
    "manager"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "calendar system",
    "meeting notes",
    "action-item tracker",
    "shared document repository"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "improvement request",
    "equipment issue summary",
    "meeting agenda",
    "vendor proposal"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "meeting minutes",
    "action-item list",
    "owner and due date assignments",
    "updated improvement proposal"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Prepare agenda and issue summary",
      "actor": "equipment engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Schedule meeting with vendor",
      "actor": "meeting organizer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Discuss improvement options",
      "actor": "equipment engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Record decisions and open questions",
      "actor": "meeting organizer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Assign action-item owners and due dates",
      "actor": "manager"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Share meeting summary",
      "actor": "meeting organizer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Track action-item progress",
      "actor": "action-item owner"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Is the proposed improvement technically feasible?",
      "branches": [
        "feasible",
        "requires revision"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Are action items clearly owned?",
      "branches": [
        "owned",
        "owner missing"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "agenda not prepared",
    "vendor proposal incomplete",
    "unclear owner",
    "missed follow-up deadline"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Meeting scheduling can be assisted by calendar availability checks."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Meeting notes can be summarized into decisions, open questions, and action items."
    },
    {
      "target": "A7",
      "rationale": "Action-item reminders and status tracking can be automated."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}

Additional constraint for this respondent: this expert answers vaguely and never commits to specifics.
Do not name any actor, system, artifact, threshold, condition or exception from the reference workflow.
Use hedged generalities such as "the person in charge usually checks it before it goes out".
Answer every question in this style, at most 30 words each.

